{"snug":{"id":"d88d0a4d-dc41-49e4-bc87-b2e2c3832297","word":"snug","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"comfortable; cosy, cozy","word":"confortável"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"I felt snug tucked up in my snug bed.","bold_text_offsets":[[7,11],[28,32]],"type":"example","id":"c19aa678-0aa5-4674-b745-f46b858257c3"},{"text":"Now, if in a stage coach in the depth of winter, when three passengers are warm and snug, a fourth, all besnowed and frozen, descends from the outside and takes place amongst them, straightway all the three passengers shift their places, uneasily pull up their cloak collars, re-arrange their \"comforters,\" feel indignantly a sensible loss of caloric—the intruder has at least made a sensation.","ref":"1848 April – 1849 October, E[dward] Bulwer-Lytton, chapter I, in The Caxtons: A Family Picture, volume II, Edinburgh; London: William Blackwood and Sons, published 1849, →OCLC, part IX, page 88:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[84,88]],"id":"438d400e-94b5-47a3-b0ea-a75eea5c945f"},{"text":"I am one of those unambitious lawyers who never addresses a jury, or in any way draws down public applause; but, in the cool tranquillity of a snug retreat, do a snug business among rich men's bonds, and mortgages, and title-deeds.","ref":"1853, Melville, Herman, Bartleby, the Scrivener, in Billy Budd, Sailor and Other Stories, New York: Penguin Books, 1968; reprint 1995 as Bartleby, page 2","id":"b97ba0f9-f6cc-47c3-81c5-a3ec036ca57b"},{"text":"That night Tarzan built a snug little bower high among the swaying branches of a giant tree, and there the tired girl slept, while in a crotch beneath her the ape-man curled, ready, even in sleep, to protect her.","ref":"1913, Edgar Rice Burroughs, The Return of Tarzan, New York: Ballantine Books, published 1963, page 214:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[26,30]],"id":"32b3edef-1ecb-4de1-a952-58c4637ad5d1"}],"links":[["Warm","warm#English"],["comfortable","comfortable"],["cosy","cosy"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"comfy"},{"word":"cosy"},{"word":"cushy"},{"word":"gemütlich"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["Warm and comfortable; cosy."],"id":"07566e7a-a2fb-4976-8622-b588ff95d84a"},{"examples":[{"text":"I am one of those unambitious lawyers who never addresses a jury, or in any way draws down public applause; but, in the cool tranquillity of a snug retreat, do a snug business among rich men's bonds, and mortgages, and title-deeds.","ref":"1853, Melville, Herman, Bartleby, the Scrivener, in Billy Budd, Sailor and Other Stories, New York: Penguin Books, 1968; reprint 1995 as Bartleby, page 2","id":"3c26bd51-621f-4025-bbd7-e4610cbaa137"}],"links":[["Satisfactory","satisfactory"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"acceptable"},{"word":"good enough"},{"word":"acceptable","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory"},{"word":"adequate","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory"},{"word":"all right","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory"},{"word":"average","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory"},{"word":"close enough","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory"},{"word":"close enough for government work","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory","tags":["US","pejorative"]},{"word":"close enough for horseshoes and hand grenades","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory"},{"word":"decent","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory"},{"word":"favoursome","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory","tags":["obsolete"]},{"word":"fair","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory"},{"word":"fine","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory","tags":["informal"]},{"word":"jake","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory","tags":["slang"]},{"word":"good enough","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory"},{"word":"good enough for government work","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory","tags":["US","pejorative"]},{"word":"hunky dory","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory","tags":["informal"]},{"word":"kosher","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory"},{"word":"mustn't grumble","source":"Thesaurus:satisfactory","tags":[